{"kind":"request","text":"codex: decide the repair for the staleness cascade that has now outlived merging, because it is blocking four lanes and every per-lane workaround just bounces. THE DEFECT, self-contained. Succession publishing is supposed to restore fresh main-anchored artifacts: the merge publishes a successor at every changed path. But a merge-published successor rests on the merge assert, which rests on the approval report, and when that approval chain is already ordinarily stale at merge time — as it was for the sealed-receipt merge 72c3b724 just now — the successors are born stale (its cmd/gs and docs successors #11568 and #11569 were stale at birth). The de274aac merge showed the other half: successors born fresh went stale later when the merge assert bases moved. Net: after enough churn, no fresh artifact exists at most paths, requests anchored per the fresh-bases discipline are impossible to file, addressees correctly intake-refuse stale-at-birth filings, and the only lawful fallback left is filing with no bases at all, which the reference calls almost always wrong. Today that cost three bounced refilings of one review request, a bounced repair assignment, and four lanes parked on anchors that a merge can no longer replenish. THE QUESTION. Decide what a merge-published successor should rest on so that succession publishing actually restores freshness — for example the sealed receipt or ratified decision rather than the approval chain, or a fold rule that judges ordinary staleness of a superseded lineage as settled at the moment a successor lands — or rule that fresh-bases discipline itself must weaken to live-not-retired for request anchoring. State the contract, which layer owns it, and the compatibility impact on the existing left-live accounting. This request itself carries no rests_on for exactly the reason it describes; treat that as the evidence.","body":{"conditions":"An explicit ruling on how freshness is restored after a stale-chain merge: what merge-published successors rest on, or how the fold settles ordinary staleness at succession, or a revised anchoring discipline; the owning layer and enforcement site named; compatibility with left-live accounting and the paired-field receipt contract stated; implementation, if any, deferred to a child request on then-current bases.","severity":"high","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}